This is a reposting of the termcap entry for the Televideo 970 revised to work
with Version E firmware.  The earlier termcap entry I posted was for version D
firmware.  The two firmware versions are not completely compatible.
  We acquired the version E roms from Televideo after complaining that one of
our terminals locks up when the keyboard is used when the computer is sending
to the terminal.  Alas, that did not fix the problem.
  None of the terminals really works well at 19,200 baud.  The visible bell
given here only marginally works. This was the same visible bell given with the
Revision D termcap version but works much worse with the revision E firmware.
The main symptom is that one gets no visible bell.  Inserting padding
characters tends to put crud on the screen. If anyone has a better visible bell
I would like to to know.  Possibly some of the entries could use padding, but I have not had the time or the will-power to do the exhaustive testing to find
out which one's and how much. Again if anyone does this I would like to know.
Bill Sebok	Princeton Univ. Astrophysics
